The vertical electrical sounding (VES) at Tigidam-street, Bori Metropolis, reveals a five-layer subsurface profile. The resistivity sequence begins at 1148 ohm-m (Layer 1), increases to 2087 ohm-m (Layer 2), and subsequently decreases to 808 ohm-m (Layer 3). The resistivity then rises through Layer 4 (1896 ohm-m) and continues upward into Layer 5 (4854 ohm-m).

Following the curve-type notation rules, the transitions are as follows: 1-2-3 follows a K pattern (increase then decrease), 2-3-4 follows an H pattern (decrease then increase), and 3-4-5 follows an A pattern (continuous increase). This results in a KHA-type curve, which is consistent with the classification currently recorded on file.

